# The toolchain the kernel is built with (tools/fetch-wolf,
# tools/fetch-lupin; tools/lib.sh's load_wolf_pin takes one of two
# shapes).
#
# px01: a RELEASE pin, the archive BY DIGEST. px02 and kw10 built
# wolf-lang eb955c3b and then 6a4e6151 from source for kw06-kw09 (int
# and pointer, volatile, exact layout, module state, sections), which
# no release carried; 0.2.23 carries them all (px05). No compiler
# source moved between 6a4e6151 and the tag (only kw10's spec, witness
# and gates and r28's version and pairing), so the kernels are the
# same bytes. px07 moves the pin to 0.2.24 (wolf-lang 294d626d, release
# 404332628), which carries kw11's raw-pointer atomics the scheduler's
# spinlock is built on (and kw12's allocator hook, px06's). px10 moves
# it to 0.2.25 (wolf-lang 6710f9e0, release 406122367): s214's #598,
# #600 and #601 fixes (loads and stores of foreign memory are no longer
# forwarded across a call that may write it; release keeps a branch on
# the top half of `u64 >> k`). px16 moves it to 0.2.26 (wolf-lang
# 89dc1394, release 408143286): `-> never` (#572), `!` on integers
# (#575), `p[i].f = v` (#577) and `m.K` (#579), which retire four of
# pax's workarounds. px21a moves it to 0.2.27 (wolf-lang 0ddda6b7,
# release 409367590): s223's `wolf_rt_ambient_get`/`_set`, which let
# the scheduler carry each thread's ambient region across a switch
# (wolf-lang#611), and s221's `ffi` capability, which every package
# that declares C now lists (kernel/wolf.pkg, tests/mkw.d/kernel/wolf.pkg,
# user/play/wolf.pkg). The archive carries a `std/` beside `wolf` since
# this release; a freestanding build reads none, and nothing here
# stages another over it. tools/fetch-wolf stages the x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
# archive, refuses on a sha256 mismatch and on a `--version` whose pin
# clause is not WOLF_PIN_COMMIT's first 7 hex, and never builds.
WOLF_VERSION=0.2.27
WOLF_URL=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/wolf-lang/releases/download/v0.2.27/wolf-0.2.27-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz
WOLF_SHA256=5e17eebed7ffbb3ee10bc669c653145903db7f591f250a096f791e4e6f377001
WOLF_PIN_COMMIT=0ddda6b7ab9f899aeeea13a66b3427f8422b8a0f
# lupin, M-KW step 6's second machine, from its release BY DIGEST:
# 0.1.50 (wolf-interp 32b970da, release 409303515), 0.2.27's pairing
# (px21a; 0.1.49, wolf-interp f516a5f4, from px16; 0.1.48 from px10).
# px05 and px07 held it at 0.1.44, whose clap error for `--target`
# tests/mkw step 6 recorded (wolf-interp#182, fixed in 0.1.46); px10
# moves it with wolf and re-records that row.
LUPIN_VERSION=0.1.50
LUPIN_SHA256=e2867a3515d4691f073f9ef30f4fe3e0fc6201f280bf24e87a42ce66562f1d93
